<title>SWEDEN: ICE HOCKEY-SWEDEN BEAT FINLAND TWICE IN TWO DAYS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-SWEDEN BEAT FINLAND TWICE IN TWO DAYS.</headline>
<dateline>ORNSKOLDSVIK, Sweden 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden beat Finland 4-3 (0-0 1-1 3-2) in an ice hockey friendly on Wednesday, their second victory over the Finns in two days.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Sweden - Michael Nylander (35.47), Johan Lindbom (47.24), Magnus Arvedsson (48.41), Mattias Ohlund (52.31).</p>
<p>Finland - Olli Jokinen (22.16), Jarkko Varvio (44.51), Mika Nieminen (50.08).</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,103.</p>
<p>Sweden won the first game 7-4 in Stockholm on Tuesday.  REUTER  162029 GMT apr 97</p>
